/-!
# The linked `mpn_add_n_loop_owned` and `mpn_sub_n_loop_owned` objects as literals

The Lean fork (spitters/lean4, branch `catcrypt-mpn-4.36.0` at `bd336156`) links
`src/runtime/catcrypt/mpn_add_n_loop_owned.o` (1048 bytes, SHA-256 `3235324f…`) and
`src/runtime/catcrypt/mpn_sub_n_loop_owned.o` (1104 bytes, SHA-256 `b97bd9cf…`). They are the
objects `MpnLoopBytesEmit.objBytes` emits at the base for `MpnLoopFrontEmit.addLprogFront` and
`subLprogFront` (same SHA-256; also the files `crates/catcrypt-mpn/obj/` of this repository).
The theorems about them are stated about these bytes, given here as literals.

## Main results

* `addObj_eq`, `subObj_eq`: each object is the single-leaf ELF object of the encoder's wrapper
  (`ElfObject.buildElfObjectMulti`) around its function bytes `addText` / `subText`.
* `addText_decode`, `subText_decode`: those bytes decode to `addDec` / `subDec`: prologue,
  zero-trip branch, a do-while loop of one straight trip, epilogue.
-/

